## System Design

The DOCX Template → Bulk DOCX/PDF Generator is designed as an asynchronous, storage-driven backend system that supports template ingestion, dynamic field extraction, single document generation, and large-scale bulk processing. The architecture prioritizes responsiveness, reliability, and safe file handling.

### Core Components

API Service

Handles client interactions including template uploads, field inspection requests, single-fill exports, bulk job submissions, and artifact downloads. The API layer validates inputs, enforces authorization, and persists metadata.

Template Ingestion Service

Processes uploaded DOCX templates, performs format validation, stores raw templates in object storage, and triggers field extraction workflows.

Field Extraction Service

Parses templates to detect placeholders or merge fields. Extracted fields are normalized and stored for reuse. This service ensures templates are decoupled from document generation logic.

Bulk Job Orchestrator

Responsible for coordinating bulk runs initiated via CSV or sheet uploads. It creates BulkRun and BulkRow records, pushes jobs to the queue, and manages execution state.

Job Queue

Decouples heavy document generation tasks from user requests. Bulk processing, retries, and exports are executed asynchronously to avoid blocking API responses.

Worker Services

Consume queued jobs and perform document generation. Workers fetch templates, inject row-specific data, generate DOCX/PDF outputs, upload artifacts, and update row status.

Export / Packaging Service

Aggregates generated artifacts into ZIP archives and produces per-row reports. This service handles packaging logic separately from generation workflows.

Object Storage

Stores templates, generated documents, ZIP files, and reports. Object storage is chosen for scalability, durability, and efficient large file handling.

Database (PostgreSQL)

Stores relational metadata including templates, template versions, fields, bulk runs, row statuses, artifacts, and job events.

---

