---

## Bulk Storage Strategy

- Templates stored in object storage using versioned paths
- CSV inputs stored temporarily with lifecycle policies
- Generated DOCX/PDF artifacts stored per row
- ZIP archives generated after completion
- Cleanup policies remove temporary inputs and failed artifacts
- Storage paths structured by user/tenant isolation

Example:

/storage/{user_id}/templates/{template_id}/v{n}
/storage/{user_id}/bulk/{bulk_run_id}/row_{n}.pdf

---

## Reliability & Failure Handling

- Bulk runs tracked independently from rows
- Each row processed as an isolated unit of work
- Partial success supported without aborting entire run
- Failed rows retried with exponential backoff
- Row-level status allows resumable bulk runs
- Idempotent job execution prevents duplicate artifacts
- Job events enable auditability and debugging

---

## Security Considerations

- Template isolation per user or tenant
- Strict authorization for template and artifact access
- Safe download strategy via signed URLs
- Anti-path traversal validation on file operations
- Input validation for CSV/sheet uploads
- No direct filesystem exposure
- Malware scanning for uploaded templates (future enhancement)

---

## Processing Flow

1. User uploads DOCX template
2. Template ingestion validates and stores file
3. Field extraction parses placeholders
4. User performs single-fill or bulk upload
5. BulkRun + BulkRow records created
6. Jobs pushed to queue
7. Workers generate documents per row
8. Artifacts uploaded to storage
9. ZIP + reports generated
10. Final statuses updated

